.Dd November 22, 2026
.Dt NATIVE-PATH-CHECK 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm native-path-check
.Nd check benchmark records against the native-path registry
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -registry Ar file
.Op Fl -jsonl
.Ar bench-history.json
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads a
.Pa bench-history.json
document and checks every entry of its
.Dq records
list against the native-path registry.
.Pp
The rule: if the native underpinnings exist, the workload is native.
A Linuxulator run where a native path exists is invalid.
Where no native path exists yet, a Linuxulator run is kept, but marked as a
last resort.
.Pp
The registry lists, for each pair of card and backend, whether a native
.Fx
path exists.
Every record carries
.Dq path
(native or linuxulator) and
.Dq path_status
(native, superseded or last-resort).
One violation is reported per record and rule broken:
.Bl -tag -width "superseded-without-native"
.It Li record-invalid
The entry of
.Dq records
is not an object.
.It Li field-type
.Dq path ,
.Dq path_status ,
.Dq card
or
.Dq backend
or
.Dq superseded_by
is present but not a string.
One violation is reported per record, naming every such field.
.It Li field-missing
The record has no
.Dq card
or no
.Dq backend ,
or neither.
The message names the missing fields.
.It Li path-missing
The record has no
.Dq path .
.It Li path-invalid
.Dq path
is neither native nor linuxulator.
.It Li unknown-pair
The pair of card and backend is not in the registry.
Fix the record or add the pair to the registry file.
.It Li native-without-path
A native record, but the registry says the pair has no native path.
.It Li status-invalid
A path_status that is not native, superseded or last-resort; a native
record whose path_status is not native; or a linuxulator record without a native
path whose path_status is not last-resort.
.It Li linux-where-native
A linuxulator record where the registry says a native path exists, whose
path_status is not superseded.
.It Li superseded-without-native
A superseded linuxulator record that does not name its successor.
A superseded record needs a string field
.Dq superseded_by
which is contained in the
.Dq source
of some native record with the same card, backend and model, dated on or after
the superseded record.
The message says which part failed.
.El
.Pp
By default one JSON document is printed on standard output with the keys
version, status (ok, violations or error), checked, counts (native and
linuxulator), violations and error.
Each violation has index, date, card, backend, path, path_status, rule and
detail.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--registry file"
.It Fl -registry Ar file
Read the registry from
.Ar file
instead of the default.
.It Fl -jsonl
Print one JSON line per violation, then one summary line with the same keys as
the document, without violations.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage, with the resolved default registry path, and exit.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "docs/native-paths.json"
.It Pa docs/native-paths.json
The default registry, found relative to the directory of the script
.Pq Pa ../docs/native-paths.json .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 3n
.It 0
Every record passes (status ok).
.It 1
At least one violation (status violations).
.It 2
Usage error, or the registry or input is unreadable or invalid (status error).
A registry is invalid when it lacks
.Dq paths ,
its version is not 1, an entry has a non-string card or backend or a
non-boolean native, or a pair appears twice.
A history is invalid when it has no records, or lacks
.Dq records ,
or when that is not a list.
With
.Fl -jsonl
anywhere on the command line, even a usage error is printed as one JSON line.
Without it, a usage error is also written in plain text to standard error.
An unexpected internal failure is reported as status error, exit 2.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check the benchmark history:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
native-path-check bench-history.json
.Ed
.Pp
List only the violations, one per line:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
native-path-check --jsonl bench-history.json
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Pa docs/llm.md ,
.Pa docs/native-paths.json
